WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:06.482
Einstein was deeply absorbed in his
research.

00:00:06.622 --> 00:00:16.116
He spent 33 days working intensely on
one problem.

00:00:16.256 --> 00:00:27.207
He did not sleep or eat, or even pause
to blink.

00:00:27.347 --> 00:00:32.402
Yet despite his efforts, success
eluded him.

00:00:32.542 --> 00:00:43.209
At such a moment, it is tempting to
give up.

00:00:43.349 --> 00:00:52.535
Einstein had no spiritual guide beside
him.

00:00:52.675 --> 00:01:06.143
He did not have the support of a
realized soul.

00:01:06.283 --> 00:01:14.143
Even so, he believed in a higher
power.

00:01:14.283 --> 00:01:20.512
With that faith, he turned to prayer.

00:01:20.652 --> 00:01:25.286
He sought the strength to continue.

00:01:25.426 --> 00:01:36.286
For 33 days, he had struggled without
success.

00:01:36.426 --> 00:01:44.286
Still, he did not give up.

00:01:44.426 --> 00:01:45.916
Instead, he prayed to God.

00:01:46.056 --> 00:01:54.808
After 72 hours of intense prayer,
inspiration came.

00:01:54.948 --> 00:02:03.658
The ideas he needed began to become
clear.

00:02:03.798 --> 00:02:13.658
He wrote down those insights and
formulated his theory.

00:02:13.798 --> 00:02:24.658
Overwhelmed with joy, he began dancing
in his laboratory.

00:02:24.798 --> 00:02:32.824
He felt the joy of a connection with
God.

00:02:32.964 --> 00:02:42.654
He went outside to share his happiness
with his fellow scientists.

00:02:42.794 --> 00:02:48.841
His colleagues asked why he was
dancing.

00:02:48.981 --> 00:02:53.841
Was he celebrating his scientific
discovery?

00:02:53.981 --> 00:02:56.841
His joy was not only about the theory.

00:02:56.981 --> 00:03:03.207
He was rejoicing because God had heard
his prayer.

00:03:03.347 --> 00:03:15.441
He discovered the theory in 1914.

00:03:15.581 --> 00:03:24.444
He kept it private for several years.

00:03:24.584 --> 00:03:30.878
Later, he shared it with scientists
close to him.

00:03:31.018 --> 00:03:39.412
In 1924, he finally released it
publicly.

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:52.322
In 1925, a ceremony was arranged to
honor him.

00:03:52.462 --> 00:04:02.763
He was invited without being told that
he was the guest of honor.

00:04:02.903 --> 00:04:14.777
He arrived and took his place among
the audience.

00:04:14.917 --> 00:04:23.696
The organizers announced that they had
gathered to honor Einstein.

00:04:23.836 --> 00:04:30.220
Only then did he realize the ceremony
was for him.

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:44.117
They praised his research and his
contribution to the world.

00:04:44.257 --> 00:04:56.117
He stopped them before they presented
the honor.

00:04:56.257 --> 00:05:05.789
He wanted to explain who truly
deserved the credit.

00:05:05.929 --> 00:05:18.744
He said his own intelligence alone had
not brought him success.

00:05:18.884 --> 00:05:23.744
Even after 33 days, the answer had not
come.

00:05:23.884 --> 00:05:34.430
Then he prayed, and God gave him
inspiration.

00:05:34.570 --> 00:05:48.430
He attributed the achievement to
divine grace, not to himself.

00:05:48.570 --> 00:06:00.430
He held up an image of God and offered
the first honor to Him.

00:06:00.570 --> 00:06:07.430
His success, he said, had come through
God's grace.

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:19.347
He also credited his fellow scientists
for their support.

00:06:19.487 --> 00:06:25.157
Only after God and his colleagues
would he accept any honor.

00:06:25.297 --> 00:06:37.464
Though he had no spiritual guide, he
placed God above himself.

00:06:37.604 --> 00:06:43.189
He also valued the support of his
companions.

00:06:43.329 --> 00:06:50.415
This is the humility we should learn.

00:06:50.555 --> 00:06:59.415
Whatever abilities we possess are
gifts.

00:06:59.555 --> 00:07:07.881
Our intelligence, strength, and
understanding come through divine
grace.

00:07:08.021 --> 00:07:17.881
We must also remember those who help
us progress.

00:07:18.021 --> 00:07:30.780
Remain humble, and never forget the
grace and guidance behind our success.

